From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 02:32:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 05/44] qwen27: run a looped checkpoint's executions and its
 two-stream mHC on Metal

The 27B engine iterated physical layers. A SenseNova-Loop checkpoint declares a
shared-weight loop (layers [4,28) run twice: 56 executions from 32 weight sets)
and manifold-constrained hyper-connections over that range, so the config now
reads loop_settings and mhc through the shared loop_schedule plan and the runner
indexes its KV and recurrent caches by **execution** rather than by physical
block: 14 attention slots and 42 GDN slots for this model, each visit with its
own state. The GDN pool's layer count follows the plan.

Kernels qwen27/mhc.metal: branch (rms over the flattened streams, one simdgroup
an output's dot product, sigmoid pre, 2*sigmoid post, log-space Sinkhorn over the
2x2 map, and the branch the sublayer runs on), merge (mix . streams + post *
branch), and the window's enter/leave boundaries. Coefficients are rounded to
bf16 before use, as the reference casts them. tf-qwen27-mhc-check compares all
four against a CPU reference of the same arithmetic: merge, enter and leave are
bit-identical and branch is exact.
